name conceptnet-assertions
# One edge on every line, five fields parted by tabs, no header row. ConceptNet's documentation (Downloads):
#   "The five fields of each line are: The URI of the whole edge; The relation expressed by the edge; The node at the
#    start of the edge; The node at the end of the edge; A JSON structure of additional information about the edge, such as its weight"
#
# (URI hierarchy) "Every object in ConceptNet has a URI that is structured like a path"; "Concept URIs contain the
# text of the concept, with spaces replaced by underscores"; a concept has "the initial /c", "a part that indicates
# its language", "a part with the concept text", and "an optional fourth component gives the part of speech"; what
# follows it the page does not name. A URI is ConceptNet's address for a term: the term is the text itself, the word any
# other witness speaks of, and what the address says of it (its language, its part of speech) is said of the term.
# /c/en/ice_cream/n is the term "ice cream", of which ConceptNet says en and n. A relation's URI, /r/IsA, is the
# relation IsA (/r/dbpedia/genre, the relation dbpedia/genre).
#
# (Edges) The edge is the claim [start, relation, end]: the line is that claim. "sources: the sources that, when
# combined, say that this assertion should be true": each contributor among them is a witness of its own and says
# the edge; an edge that names no contributor is said by ConceptNet. What else the JSON says of the edge (its weight,
# the sentence it was read from and the surface forms of its two ends) ConceptNet says of the edge. The edge's own
# URI is its start, relation and end again; the dataset, licence, process and activity are ConceptNet's bookkeeping.
match assertions.csv

tier edge by \n
names uri rel start end json
tier field by \t
part rel by / pieces 2
part start by / space _
part end by / space _
part json by object

# ExternalURL is no relation between terms: its end is a URL of the term on another site, which split at its slashes
# made wiki and en.wiktionary.org things of their own (about 49M attestations). Those edges are not read.
where rel is-not /r/ExternalURL
omit uri dataset license process activity
content rel start end weight surfaceText surfaceStart surfaceEnd
own contributor

thing edge start/3 rel/2 end/3
itself edge by json/sources/contributor
attest edge json
pair edge start/2 start/4 of start/3
pair edge end/2 end/4 of end/3
